<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $344.6 mln Nov 6.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $344.6 mln Nov 6.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $344.6 million surplus on November 6 according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 6</p>
<p>Exports: $176.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $159.3 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $696.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $369.3 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $344.6 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $753.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $670.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.981 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $934.7 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.129 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-248-5400</p>
